            <ArticleTitle>Dual source CT: cardio-pulmonary applications.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>77-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dual source CT is a last generation scanner which allows for coronary imaging without beta-blocker because high quality images are feasible even at high heart rates. Furthermore, with this equipment, dual energy becomes possible in a single acquisition and triple rule-out imaging can be performed in clinical routine. The radiation dose remains limited in comparison with single-source CT because of different efficient mechanisms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
